<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cross Group</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">692</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cross Group is a set of three temple-pyramids at Palenque, the Temple of the Cross, the Temple of the Foliated Cross and the Temple of the Sun, dedicated in 692 by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kinich-kan-bahlam-ii">K'inich Kan B'ahlam II</a>. Their carved panels show the king with his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kinich-janaab-pakal">Pakal</a> and record the mythical origins of the city's patron gods and dynasty.</p></div>
